{
  "_comment": [
    "Wiring for the NCBI MCP server. Copy the 'mcpServers' block into your",
    "client's MCP config (Claude Code: .mcp.json in the repo root).",
    "Replace /ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO with this checkout's path -- most clients do",
    "not launch the server from the repo directory.",
    "",
    "NCBI_EMAIL: who NCBI contacts if this server misbehaves. They email",
    "before blocking, so a wrong address turns a warning into an outage.",
    "",
    "NCBI_API_KEY: optional. Raises the limit from 3 to 10 requests/second.",
    "Free from https://account.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/settings/. Leave it out and",
    "the server paces itself at 3/sec.",
    "",
    "NCBI_MAX_RPS: optional, lowers the rate. The limit is per IP, so if",
    "several people on one network each run a copy, they share one budget --",
    "set this to 3 divided by the number of copies."
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "ncbi": {
      "command": "/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/federated-data-ecosystem-assistant/.venv/bin/python",
      "args": ["-m", "ncbi_mcp"],
      "cwd": "/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/federated-data-ecosystem-assistant",
      "env": {
        "NCBI_EMAIL": "you@example.org"
      }
    }
  }
}
